<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigismund II Augustus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1572">1572</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigismund II Augustus was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, the last of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-dynasty">Jagiellonian dynasty</a>, who died in 1572. He presided over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> of 1569, which formally created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. His death without an heir led to the system of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elective-monarchy">elective monarchy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sigismund-ii-augustus.jpg" alt="Sigismund II Augustus" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cranach_the_Younger_Sigismund_II_Augustus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
